6,"ps_ratio":13,"fcf_to_ev":1.92,"fcf_to_mcap":1.92,"liab_to_assets":44.1,"cash_to_assets":12.8,"current_ratio":1.24,"roe":11.4,"roa":6.4,"moat":{"ticker":"PSMT","period":"2026Q4","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 在拉丁美洲的折扣倉儲會員制零售市場中，建立了一定的品牌認知度，但其品牌力相較於全球性的零售巨頭或特定品類的領導者仍有差距。其定價策略主要依賴於提供具競爭力的價格，吸引對價格敏感的消費者，而非透過品牌溢價。這意味著其定價權相對有限，容易受到競爭對手的價格戰影響。雖然其會員模式有助於鎖定部分客戶，但品牌本身並未形成強大的情感連結或獨特性，因此在品牌護城河方面，表現屬中等水平。","comment_en":"PriceSmart has established some brand recognition in the discount warehouse membership retail market in Latin America, but its brand strength still lags behind global retail giants or category-specific leaders. Its pricing strategy primarily relies on offering competitive prices to attract price-sensitive consumers, rather than commanding brand premiums. This implies its pricing power is relatively limited and susceptible to competitors' price wars. While its membership model helps retain some customers, the brand itself has not formed strong emotional connections or unique appeal, thus its brand moat is considered moderate."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 的業務模式屬於傳統的零售業，不涉及高度依賴專利技術或特殊監管許可的領域。其營運主要受一般性商業法規約束，並無顯著的專利或特許權構成其核心競爭壁壘。因此，在專利與監管這一維度上，PriceSmart 幾乎沒有護城河可言，得分極低，反映了該領域的低進入門檻和高度可複製性。","comment_en":"PriceSmart's business model falls within traditional retail and does not involve areas heavily reliant on patented technology or special regulatory licenses. Its operations are primarily governed by general commercial regulations, and there are no significant patents or exclusive licenses forming its core competitive barrier. Therefore, in terms of patents and regulatory aspects, PriceSmart has virtually no moat, resulting in a very low score, reflecting the low barriers to entry and high replicability in this domain."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 的轉換成本主要體現在其會員制度上。一旦消費者支付了年費並習慣了其購物模式，例如尋找特價商品和利用會員折扣，轉換到其他零售商可能會帶來不便或額外的成本（如重新適應購物習慣、失去會員權益）。然而，由於其商品種類相對標準化，且競爭對手提供類似的折扣或便利性，這種轉換成本並非不可逾越。因此，其轉換成本壁壘屬於中等偏弱。","comment_en":"PriceSmart's switching costs are mainly reflected in its membership system. Once consumers pay the annual fee and become accustomed to its shopping model, such as seeking out special offers and utilizing member discounts, switching to other retailers might involve inconvenience or additional costs (like readjusting shopping habits or losing membership benefits). However, as its product range is relatively standardized and competitors offer similar discounts or conveniences, these switching costs are not insurmountable. Therefore, its switching cost barrier is considered moderately weak."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 的業務模式並未展現出顯著的網絡效應。其會員制雖然能帶來一定的客戶黏性，但並非典型的「使用者越多，價值越大」的網絡效應。例如，一個會員的加入並不會直接提升其他會員的購物體驗或價值。其營運依賴於商品採購和門店運營效率，而非用戶間的互動或數據積累帶來的規模效益。因此，在網絡效應方面，PriceSmart 的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"PriceSmart's business model does not exhibit significant network effects. While its membership model provides some customer stickiness, it's not a typical 'the more users, the greater the value' network effect. For instance, the addition of one member does not directly enhance the shopping experience or value for other members. Its operations rely on procurement and store operational efficiency, rather than economies of scale derived from user interactions or data accumulation. Consequently, PriceSmart's moat in terms of network effects is very weak."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 作為拉丁美洲領先的倉儲式會員制零售商，其規模經濟效應顯著。龐大的採購量使其能夠從供應商處獲得更優惠的價格，並將節省的成本轉嫁給會員，從而維持其價格競爭力。此外，其標準化的營運模式和對商品種類的嚴格篩選，也進一步降低了單店的運營成本。這種規模帶來的成本優勢，是其區別於小型零售商並吸引價格敏感客戶的關鍵壁壘。","comment_en":"As a leading warehouse membership retailer in Latin America, PriceSmart benefits from significant economies of scale. Its large purchasing volume allows it to secure more favorable prices from suppliers, passing these cost savings onto its members and thus maintaining its price competitiveness. Furthermore, its standardized operating model and strict product selection further reduce per-store operational costs. This scale-driven cost advantage is a key barrier that differentiates it from smaller retailers and attracts price-sensitive customers."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 在拉丁美洲特定市場的深耕，使其在該區域建立了獨特的地理優勢和市場滲透率。其對當地消費者偏好、物流網絡和法規環境的深入了解，是新進入者難以快速複製的。雖然其業務模式本身並非獨一無二，但在特定區域市場內，其多年建立的營運網絡、供應鏈關係和品牌聲譽，構成了相當於「利基寡占」的壁壘，使其在目標市場中具有較強的競爭地位。","comment_en":"PriceSmart's deep penetration in specific Latin American markets has established a unique geographical advantage and market share. Its in-depth understanding of local consumer preferences, logistics networks, and regulatory environments is difficult for new entrants to replicate quickly. While its business model itself is not unique, within its target regional markets, its long-established operational network, supply chain relationships, and brand reputation constitute a barrier akin to a 'niche oligopoly,' giving it a strong competitive position."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 在其倉儲式會員制零售模式上展現了高度的營運效率。透過精選商品種類、簡化陳列方式以及會員制的預收費模式，公司能夠有效控制庫存、降低營銷成本並預測現金流。其對供應鏈的管理和對營運流程的標準化，確保了在提供低價的同時，仍能維持健康的利潤率和穩定的自由現金流。這種卓越的營運效率是其核心競爭力之一。","comment_en":"PriceSmart demonstrates high operational efficiency in its warehouse membership retail model. By carefully selecting product categories, simplifying display methods, and utilizing the pre-paid membership model, the company effectively controls inventory, reduces marketing costs, and forecasts cash flow. Its supply chain management and standardization of operational processes ensure that it can maintain healthy profit margins and stable free cash flow while offering low prices. This operational excellence is one of its core competitive strengths."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 在資本配置方面表現穩健。公司能夠持續產生正向自由現金流，並將其用於支持業務擴張、償還債務以及適度的股東回報。其管理層在評估新市場進入、門店開設和營運優化方面的決策，顯示出對資本回報率的關注。雖然其成長潛力可能不如科技公司，但其在零售業內謹慎而務實的資本配置策略，有助於維持公司的長期穩健發展和股東價值。","comment_en":"PriceSmart exhibits sound capital allocation. The company consistently generates positive free cash flow, which it uses to support business expansion, repay debt, and provide moderate shareholder returns. Its management's decisions in evaluating new market entries, store openings, and operational optimizations reflect a focus on return on capital. While its growth potential may not match that of tech companies, its prudent and pragmatic capital allocation strategy within the retail sector contributes to the company's long-term stable development and shareholder value."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 的會員制度是其客戶保留策略的核心。透過收取年費，公司不僅獲得了穩定的預收收入，也培養了會員的忠誠度。會員一旦習慣了 PriceSmart 的購物模式和價格優勢，且其商品組合能持續滿足基本需求，轉換到其他零售商的意願就會降低。雖然不是絕對的鎖定，但會員資格本身以及持續提供的價值，構成了較強的客戶保留壁壘。","comment_en":"PriceSmart's membership system is central to its customer retention strategy. By charging an annual fee, the company not only secures stable upfront revenue but also cultivates member loyalty. Once members become accustomed to PriceSmart's shopping model and price advantages, and if its product assortment continues to meet their basic needs, their willingness to switch to other retailers decreases. While not absolute lock-in, the membership itself and the sustained value provided constitute a relatively strong customer retention barrier."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"PriceSmart 的業務模式具有相當的持久性。倉儲式會員制零售滿足了消費者對高性價比商品的基本需求，這種需求在經濟週期中相對穩定。其在拉丁美洲市場的長期經營，證明了其商業模式能夠適應當地環境並持續獲利。儘管零售業面臨線上線下競爭和消費者習慣變遷的挑戰，但 PriceSmart 專注於特定市場和客戶群，並依賴規模和效率來維持競爭力，使其在可預見的未來，仍能保持其市場地位和盈利能力。","comment_en":"PriceSmart's business model possesses considerable durability. The warehouse membership retail model caters to consumers' fundamental need for high-value goods, a demand that remains relatively stable across economic cycles. Its long-term operations in Latin American markets demonstrate that its business model can adapt to local conditions and remain profitable. Despite the challenges of online-offline competition and evolving consumer habits in the retail sector, PriceSmart's focus on specific markets and customer segments, coupled with its reliance on scale and efficiency to maintain competitiveness, positions it to retain its market position and profitability in the foreseeable future."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"PriceSmart 在拉丁美洲市場建立了一個以規模經濟和營運效率為核心的護城河。其倉儲式會員制模式，雖然在品牌力與網絡效應上較為薄弱，但在成本優勢、客戶保留和特定區域市場的滲透上表現突出，構成了類似「收費橋」的價值傳遞模式，讓消費者為其提供的價格與便利性付費。其持久的業務模式和穩健的資本配置，使其在可預見的未來能持續為股東創造價值，屬於一個具有堅固護城河的價值型投資標的。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"PriceSmart has established a moat in the Latin American market centered on economies of scale and operational efficiency. While its warehouse membership model is relatively weaker in brand power and network effects, it excels in cost advantages, customer retention, and penetration in specific regional markets, forming a value-transfer model akin to a 'toll bridge' where consumers pay for the price and convenience it offers. Its durable business model and sound capital allocation enable it to continue creating shareholder value in the foreseeable future, making it a value investment target with a solid moat.","evidenceHash":"595ed4349be159430eba1e86f8e49723e826fe9164cb05bdd676ef557489dd07","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"595ed4349be159430eba1e86f8e49723e826fe9164cb05bdd676ef557489dd07","currentEvidenceHash":"595ed4349be159430eba1e86f8e49723e826fe9164cb05bdd676ef557489dd07"},"fScore":{"score":6,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-08-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T12:41:57.615Z","evidenceHash":"949fc3627d6681969b344607c06583e307264e929fe25c9c8f5048624b5c5bbf"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-08-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T12:41:57.615Z","evidenceHash":"949fc3627d6681969b344607c06583e307264e929fe25c9c8f5048624b5c5bbf"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PSMT.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PSMT.png","website":"https://www.pricesmart.com","ceo":"David N. Price","full_time_employees":"13000","description":"PriceSmart, Inc. owns and operates U.S.-style membership shopping warehouse clubs in the United States, Central America, the Caribbean, and Colombia. The company provides basic and private label merchandise and consumable and non-consumable products under the Member’s Selection brand, including groceries, cleaning supplies, health and beauty aids, meat, produce, deli, seafood, and poultry. It also offers electronics, large and small appliances, automotive, hardware, sporting goods, seasonal products, clothing, domestic, and home furnishing products. In addition, the company offers food and bakery services, as well as health services, such as optical, audiology, and pharmacy. Further, it operates an e-commerce platform, as well as offers curbside pickup and delivery services. PriceSmart, Inc. was incorporated in 1994 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","description_en":"PriceSmart, Inc. owns and operates U.S.-style membership shopping warehouse clubs in the United States, Central America, the Caribbean, and Colombia. The company provides basic and private label merchandise and consumable and non-consumable products under the Member’s Selection brand, including groceries, cleaning supplies, health and beauty aids, meat, produce, deli, seafood, and poultry. It also offers electronics, large and small appliances, automotive, hardware, sporting goods, seasonal products, clothing, domestic, and home furnishing products. In addition, the company offers food and bakery services, as well as health services, su